    "description": "Divert, Inc. is a food waste processing and circularity platform serving grocery retailers and other commercial food supply-chain participants. Its customers use the platform to reduce waste disposal volumes, recover unsold food, and produce renewable natural gas and other recovered outputs. The model is asset-heavy and infrastructure-oriented, with value supported by processing facilities, logistics, and contracted commercial relationships. Public company materials state that Divert was founded in 2007 and has been building a national network to process unsold food at industrial scale. The reviewed materials did not disclose company revenue or the current ownership percentages held by GIC and other investors. Divert announced a major 2021 investment round led by Ara Partners, GIC, and Ontario Power Generation and later disclosed broader business momentum as it continued to scale its network.",
